p.write_text('''# Episode 9 research checkpoint\n\nBest fully measured source remains **432_episode7_schedule_bounds**, historical raw **0.03942903473265081 s**, score **0.924392250394403**, source hash **7d3f1dd18cf04a39aba10066b90def10384a1f4fd0f9b5562d00d89e1639a354**. All30 cases/all270 quality records pass; worstnRMSE0.0070259483/minrho0.999956596/mintop0.992.\n\n**Official evaluation currently pending:547_episode9_class_column_shared_vector_zero**. Candidate is temporarily installed; restore fastest complete valid source using `python /tmp/research_history/episode9_index.py --restore` after the run. Current547 hash592df6dad60e09f62656181a75ed1687b9e58c4dfa0e8ad799e2a3f4217a33b4. Shell process session90155. No own numerical work concurrent with official.\n\nCompleted official episode9 runs:497 baseline repeat raw0.049396719331950105 score0.9052785640857877 (same432 hash);515 class column-major raw0.040048826466954776 score0.9232037592590603 hashd55f04d527fb23000cd61107bdbd3facd172e52bb43a5969e195a87f3ae463d3. Both all30 valid. Originalstdout and unchanged reports archived in each source directory.\n\n51 episode9 snapshots,50 complete all30 local screens,45 local-valid sources and5 failures before latest build548-552. Builders1-10 and manifests/fullscreenJSON/logs under research_history. Local screens compare to own saved initial-source outputs from public arrays, never protected targets.\n\nFindings: unpadded Torch segment/scatter exact butslow; final retained class g-only fails1 andf-only fails5. Physical class column-major layout promising; physical point reversal not compelling. Shared unique-support setup/globalpackedmatmul allaccurate butnot consistentlyfaster. Support-sizebuckets preserveglobalhardcutoff/finiteending butslow. Class first-mean stage passes;two mean stagesfail11. Initial softkernels can omitglobalminimum shift if potential/temperaturebound<60;all30matchesbaseaccuracy. Vectorized schedule table preserves canonical np.arange effective step andmatchesexact metricprecision.\n\nCached exact empirical point variances restoreoneearliercoarse stage andimproveworstnRMSE0.006117. Withhard8/16 all30valid0.008646; pointlate4fails22,hard8late4fails13. Classlate4+earliercumulant passes0.008906,but statisticscostandfreshmedian0.042335lose.\n\nFreshround1 favored512 guardedinitialzero-shift:median0.038613 vsbase0.040559. Freshround2 favored547 exactpoint/classsetup combination:median0.038028 vsbase0.043682;5120.039156;5340.039877;5350.040429;5360.040521;5460.040407. Useofficialresultsforretention.\n\nNew substantive hypothesis built butnot screened548-552: exact first coupling row-scale cancellation. K=exp(-10C/Cmax),v=1/(m*Ksumcolumns),u=1/(n*K @ v),w=v*clamp(2-m*v*(K.T @ u),.01), expectation=mean((K*C) @ w/(K @ w)). Itremovestwo dense scalings because first rowfactor cancels final rowconditionalization. Compare originalrow-majorK,column-majorKanddensecolumnsum;548isbase432,549/552combine547. Screen next after547officialfinishes.\n\nPlanned: finish547official,screen548-552,run18syntheticpublicpermutationstress withcanonicaltargetscomputedfresh,thencompleteofficialevaluationofbest remainingpromisingcandidate(512 or coupling cancellation) andrestorefastestfullyvalid measuredsource.\n\nFrozen solve.sh SHA256bca6ef61c3a1bc0ded2aa6b2da4734b62072846def679d12a2d7ae669fc88bd1; invoke `sh ./solve.sh` (mode0444frozen). Onlymethodsubmissionchanged. No protectedassets/evaluatorcode/targets/privatecases,credentials,envvars,network,externalpackages,othertrajectoriesorsubagentsaccessed.\n''')
(root/'episode9_coupling_cancellation_derivation.md').write_text('''# Exact first-row cancellation in the current coupling expectation\n\nLet K=exp(-10 C / max(C)). The current method scales columns by v_j=1/(m sum_i K_ij), then rows by u_i=1/(n (Kv)_i). Its second column correction is a_j=clamp(2-m v_j (K^T u)_j,.01). Final row normalization computes sum_j u_i K_ij v_j a_j C_ij / sum_j u_i K_ij v_j a_j. The u_i factor cancels. Thus w=v*a and expectation is mean_i ((K*C)w)_i / (Kw)_i. No empirical points or weights have been omitted and the second correction stays unchanged. Differences from the current implementation should arise only from float32 reduction order.\n\nThis reduces full dense broadcast scalings from three to zero, replacing row/column reductions with matrix-vector products. Previous source368 cancelled only the final second-column broadcast while retaining the first row scaling. New548-552 cancel that first row scaling too; speed depends on two-core matrix-vector kernels. Do not assume the algebraic reduction implies a measured speed win.\n\nInitial unshifted soft-transform kernels use R=C-f-g. For nonnegative geometric costs, -R/eps <= (max(f)+max(g))/eps. A bound below60 keeps the largest exponential belowexp(60), and summing at most1024 terms remains within float32. Failed positive-support checks retain the original stable fallback. Class initialization from empirical squared distances satisfies an even stronger geometric bound, but the guard remains explicit.\n''')
